Files: examples/form/index.html, examples/form/main.js, examples/form/README.md (ALL NEW)

OLD_SECTION
(none — the examples/ directory had only modal/ and spa/)

NEW_SECTION
A runnable demo exercising all six FormComponents builders, following the structure of
examples/modal/ (index.html + main.js + README.md, served from the repo root with
data-library-root="../../"):
- index.html — markup for two selects (optgroup/disabled/multiple), a 3-radio group
  with axis classes, two checkboxes, date + datetime-local pickers with min/max and a
  preset value, two slide switches with data-dim/data-labels, and a file input; plus a
  "native change log" panel and live date-state lines.
- main.js — configures and autoBuild()s each builder; wires "Add option +
  refreshSelect()" and "Inject a new switch + refresh()" buttons; mirrors the date
  pickers' value/data-complete attributes via MutationObserver; logs every native
  change event through one delegated listener; exposes the builders on window.demoForm.
- README.md — run instructions and a walkthrough of what each control demonstrates.

REASON
Requested runnable example coverage for all custom form components, matching the
existing examples convention. The demo was driven end-to-end in headless Chromium
(18 scripted interaction checks, all passing, zero console errors), which also
uncovered the library defects fixed in this feature's other logs.
